🚨 Your Stage 1 Market for a Cloud Security Platform MVP:
✅ Primary Buyer Persona: Time-Poor CTOs in High-Pressure SMBs (20–200 staff)

Not security managers. Not CFOs. And definitely not COOs. Here's why:

CTOs own the problem. They carry the blame when something breaks or gets breached.

They’re overwhelmed. Especially in NZ-based SMBs—they’re firefighting, not strategy-planning.

They hate vendors. But they love tools that "just work" and free up their time.

They're cloud-native or in transition. Which means they’re vulnerable but can still be influenced before they bolt down their architecture.

🎯 Industry Sweet Spot (NZ + Global Expansion Potential):
💥 Target industries where:

Security matters. A breach = lost contracts or lawsuits.

Cloud adoption is high. No on-prem dinosaurs.

In-house security is minimal. They know enough to worry, but not enough to act.

🔪 Cut through the noise: Focus on these industries:
Industry	Why You Should Target Them
SaaS companies	Fast-moving, cloud-native, no internal SecOps team
Healthtech startups	Compliance pressure + limited security capability
Fintech / Payments	Regulated, scared of breaches, strapped for time
Digital Agencies	Handling client data, no real infosec posture
Professional Services (legal/accounting)	Cloud adoption + liability risk

✅ Bonus: All of these exist in droves in Wellington & Auckland, are plugged into LinkedIn, and many attend the same meetups/conferences.

📍 Why Wellington + Auckland?

Wellington: Public sector-adjacent, a lot of govt contractors, tech vendors, and security-conscious dev shops. Great for beta validation and reference customers.

Auckland: Bigger market, more SaaS + fintech, more investors. That’s where scale comes from.

You don’t want Christchurch (too slow). You don’t want Dunedin (too academic). You want where the action and stress is.

🧠 Ideal Pain Narrative for MVP Stage:

"I'm a CTO running a hybrid cloud mess, barely keeping up with dev demands, and now the board wants a security audit. I know we’re exposed, I just don’t have the time or headspace to deal with it. I need someone to tell me what’s wrong and help fix it without a 3-month project or 80-page report."

Your MVP must:

Identify misconfigs, exposure, compliance gaps

Give 1-click remediation or at least a playbook

Be self-serve + support optionality

Show value in under 30 minutes

🔥 Outreach Messaging Angle (Tested & Effective):

"CTO sanity check: Would you pass a security audit today?"

"Most small NZ tech teams are wide open to breach – and don’t even know it."

"You’re cloud-native but still one click away from a public S3 bucket leaking your customer data."

Use cold email + LinkedIn DMs + referrals. Build a landing page with an offer like:
“Free 30-minute Cloud Security Scan for NZ tech leaders – limited slots.”